      "message": "[error] Line 141: 🔴 Toggling a highlighted group off removes members by URI (`filter(m \u003d\u003e !peers.includes(m.uri))`), which also drops members that were selected from other conversations. Example: select `aliceDm`, then select `group` (`alice`,`bob`), then toggle `group` off — `alice` is removed even though `aliceDm` is still selected. This breaks selection consistency between chips and rows. Fix by only removing entries owned by the toggled conversation (e.g. `m.convId \u003d\u003d\u003d convId`) or by tracking per-member selection provenance/ref-count and removing a URI only when no source conversation still selects it.",
